well witnesses say soldiers in sudan  have shot dead at least five people at a  protest demanding an end to military  rule the qatar-based news network al  jazeera which had been covering the  demonstrations says its bureau chief has  been arrested the protests came after  the army set up a new ruling council  without any civilians on it it dissolved  the country's power sharing government  last month  [Applause]  they came in their thousands in defiance  of the military  across sudan the streets filled with  calls for democratic rule  they were met with violence from  security forces  protesters say live bullets were fired  this coup is demolishing the  constitution they arrest young people  just for calling for civilian rule and  democracy  we want prime minister abdallah hamduk  to be freed as well as all the  politicians ministers and activists  the prime minister is among those  detained in the october coup  demonstrators are demanding a new era in  sudanese politics as the military  tightens its grip  since 1956 this country was ruled by  three military people and they did not  change anything  we are way behind the rest of the world  we want democratic civilian rule  police deny firing at the demonstrators  but the injuries at hospitals say  otherwise  i was shot  it was in the back  there was another one just like me but  he died  god gave me some extra time  [Music]  people should not stop i was beaten but  i have to go back to protest tomorrow  it's good that i'm alive but i wanted to  be a martyr  i said goodbye before i left home  a sacrifice some see as necessary in  sudan's long struggle for democracy
 

